{
  "id": "strike_01",
  "name": "Strike",
  "cost": 1,
  "type": "attack",
  "effects": [
    {
      "type": "damage",
      "value": 6
    }
  ]
}
Enemy Schema (enemies.json)
{
  "id": "enemy_basic_01",
  "name": "Street Punk",
  "max_hp": 40,
  "intent_pattern": ["attack", "defend"]
}
Card Engine Rules
Deck → Draw pile → Hand → Discard → Exhaust
Shuffle discard into draw when empty
Max hand size: 10
Energy resets each turn
Cards resolve through action_resolver.py
Combat System Contract
Turn Flow
Player turn starts
Draw cards
Player plays cards
End turn
Enemy intent executes
Repeat
Required Public Interfaces
Deck Manager
draw_cards(n)
discard_card(card)
exhaust_card(card)
shuffle_deck()
Combat Manager
start_combat()
end_turn()
resolve_action(action)
Enemy
choose_intent()
execute_intent()
Animation Contract
Animations triggered by state strings
Example:
"idle"
"attack"
"hit"
Animator must NOT modify game logic
Audio Contract
All audio triggered through audio_manager.py
No direct sound calls in gameplay logic
Map System Contract
Map outputs graph structure
Node types:
combat
elite
shop
event
boss
Integration Rules
Modules communicate only through defined interfaces
No cross-module direct variable access
No system should assume another system’s internal logic
Testing Requirement

Each system must include:

A minimal test or simulation function
Ability to run without UI
Versioning Rule

If ANY of these change:

card schema
enemy schema
save format

Then:

Increment version in config.py
Maintain backward compatibility or migration
